lesson: 252
title: Recipes and sandwiches
level: primary-3
stars: 0
explain: A sandwich is made from 2 slices of bread with the filling in between.
explain: So the slices needed are 2 for every sandwich: first count the sandwiches, then double them.
explain: 4 children each take 3 sandwiches: 4 × 3 = 12 sandwiches, and 12 × 2 = 24 slices of bread.
vars: a=name b=name p=2..9 k=2..4
answer: p * k * 2
exercise: {a} makes {k} sandwiches for each of {p} children. How many slices of bread does {a.he} need?
exercise: For a picnic, {p} friends want {k} sandwiches each. How many slices of bread must be used?
exercise: {a}'s dad packs {k} sandwiches in each of {p} lunch boxes. How many slices of bread does he use?
exercise: The {p} players on a team each get {k} sandwiches after the match. How many slices of bread are needed?
exercise: {a} and {b} make sandwiches for a party of {p} people, {k} sandwiches for each person. How many slices of bread do they need?
exercise: making sarnies for {p} of us, {k} each. how many slices of bread
exercise: {p} kids on the trip, {k} sandwiches each, how many slices do i need mum
exercise: ok so {a}'s doing lunch for {p+1}, sorry {p} people, {k} sammies each. how many slices of bread
exercise: we're {p} at the beach n everyone wants {k} sandwiches, oh and bring the sunscreen. how many slices of bread
exercise: gotta make {k} butties each for {p} lads at footy. how many slices that is
test: How many slices of bread go into {k} sandwiches for every one of {p} hikers?
test: Each of the {p} guests will eat {k} sandwiches. What number of bread slices does the cook need?
test: {a} has to feed {p} cousins, and every cousin wants {k} cheese sandwiches. How many slices of bread will {a} take out of the bag?
test: {p} people, {k} sandwiches a head. slices of bread?
test: {a} says {p*k} slices is enough for {k} sandwiches each for {p} of us. nah. how many slices really
test: {p} kids, {k} jam sangas each, {b}'s bringing the juice. how many slices
exam: It is given that {p.words} persons are each to receive {k.words} sandwiches. Determine the aggregate number of slices of bread required for their preparation.
exam: A catering order specifies {k} sandwiches per participant for a party of {p} participants. Ascertain the total quantity of bread slices to be consumed in the fulfilment of said order.
exam: Compute the number of slices of bread necessitated by the preparation of {k} sandwiches in respect of each of {p} children.
exam: Whereas {p} attendees are to be provided with {k} sandwiches apiece, state the total number of bread slices requisite thereto.
exercise: {a}'s uncle was let go from the bakery, so he makes the picnic himself: {k} sandwiches for each of {p} children. How many slices of bread does he need?
exercise: mum's a bit stretched this week, skint basically, so it's homemade sandwiches, {k} each for {p} kids, and stop whining. how many slices of bread?
test: {a} was economical with the truth when {a.he} said the {p} campers wanted one sandwich each; they each want {k}. How many slices of bread are really needed?
